        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                "word": "calebasse",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "b8f900d2-0df3-4e84-a11f-5e815be342f9",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "calebasses"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "34efedfe-373d-386f-9cad-d9b02e807a0d",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fruit du calebassier."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Un de ces fruits, vidé et séché, et qui sert à contenir des boissons et à divers autres emplois."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Plus courant"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "627893cf-7cc9-4a66-915f-a25cb8718feb",
                                "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                                "text": "Il n’y avait dans ce lieu qu’une natte de feuilles de papaya, une calebasse pour puiser de l’eau, quelques vases de bois, une bêche, un serpent familier."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b810b166-0ab2-4bdc-87f5-c676be213f42",
                                "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                                "text": "Nous retournâmes à la hutte qui nous avait été assignée, où bientôt après le prince nous envoya une calebasse de lait et de déguet qu’il me priait d’accepter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5419c16-c6a2-4479-a905-319d431cb569",
                                "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                                "text": "Alors, la sorcière lui a donné un parchemin dans une calebasse qu’il porte toujours sur lui quand il est en mer ; mais, à sa place, il y a longtemps que j’aurais jeté au feu parchemin et tout ; ou bien je l’aurais donné à un prêtre, car qui traite avec le diable est toujours mauvais marchand."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "335fcaf2-ee30-4b08-86ae-a569c45877d3",
                                "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                                "text": "Il regarda autour de lui, vers la porte qui donnait accès à l’escalier du rez-de-chaussée, et vers le guichet de la cuisine, puis d’un geste fatigué il tira de sa poche revolver un portefeuille si incurvé et si tanné qu’il ressemblait à un fond de calebasse."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa4b63c6-42a3-499b-bdf3-23adad9842e1",
                                "sense_id": "228f6770-c096-3f85-96a4-bb6eb803ea20",
                                "text": "C’était l’unique endroit où il leur était donné de rencontrer des femmes, le plus souvent des paysannes à silhouette de calebasse, alourdies de cabas, qui martelaient le sol d’un pas endolori."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5fab3adf-9123-3ab0-88ab-ada91797aee6",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nom usuel en Afrique francophone de la plante et de son fruit, de la famille des Cucurbitaceae (Cucurbitacées), nommés Lagenaria siceraria, dont les fruits jeunes sont mangés cuits. Le fruit sec, mature et évidé est utilisé comme contenant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Afrique"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8eee07a5-c052-3274-9641-4f75bf14a247",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tête."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "8d816976-bd7e-4b35-bea6-cc465d9670c0",
                                "sense_id": "8eee07a5-c052-3274-9641-4f75bf14a247",
                                "text": "Ne rien avoir dans la calebasse (être simple d’esprit ou sot)."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "382f055a-2252-3c1b-aa8f-4d1d3c903cb4",
                        "entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Petit appareil, proche du cubilot, utilisé pour fondre des métaux en petite quantité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d30b01d3-aade-47fd-8891-b38b4c642d80",
                                "sense_id": "382f055a-2252-3c1b-aa8f-4d1d3c903cb4",
                                "text": "On les appelait alors calebassiers, du nom donné à leur rustique appareil de fusion qui composait l’essentiel de leur outillage : la calebasse portative."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "42c3fbc7-0957-432d-a405-5f2566d55500",
                                "sense_id": "382f055a-2252-3c1b-aa8f-4d1d3c903cb4",
                                "text": "À Bruxelles, la calebasse est employée pour couler de petits objets, tels qu’ornements, candélabres, statuettes, réchauds, grilles de fourneaux portatifs, fers à repasser le linge, rampes d’escaliers, etc."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2f63b75b-7252-4466-8bb6-af214a76290c",
                                "sense_id": "382f055a-2252-3c1b-aa8f-4d1d3c903cb4",
                                "text": "Dans quelques cas assez rares, et pour de grosses pièces seulement, on fond dans un petit cubilot ou dans une calebasse, on fait des moules en sable d'étuve ou en sable vert un peu séché."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e49baf0e-4e4e-4392-af68-7f286ed00b8f",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa187ff3-1f75-316b-a065-a5594285d073",
                        "target_lang_word": "calabash",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "calabash",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e25fdcb1-28da-30b7-969c-245053538d3d",
                                        "entry_id": "abfec5d9-65b5-3d19-a779-db7e170fc5ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tree (known as the calabash tree; Crescentia cujete) native to Central and South America, the West Indies, and southern Florida, bearing large, round fruit used to make containers (sense 3); the fruit of this tree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f342a864-5870-4ab6-b318-55a1e1096b67",
                                                "sense_id": "e25fdcb1-28da-30b7-969c-245053538d3d",
                                                "text": "As we were absolutely destitute of large vessels, to contain and mix liquids, we poured, by means of a tutuma (fruit of crescentia cujete, calabash), the water of the river into one of the holes of the rock. To this we added sugar, and the juice of acid fruits. In a few minutes we had an excellent beverage, which was almost a refinement of luxury in that wild spot; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c687a83c-bd4c-4243-bb57-40fd67a56eec",
                                                "sense_id": "e25fdcb1-28da-30b7-969c-245053538d3d",
                                                "text": "There was a teacher who taught children to read under a calabash tree, and this teacher's name was Goso."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "403fd2e7-d153-3476-8425-e1ea07f98b16",
                                        "entry_id": "abfec5d9-65b5-3d19-a779-db7e170fc5ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The bottle gourd (calabash vine, Lagenaria siceraria), believed to have originated in Africa, which is grown for its fruit that are used as a vegetable and to make containers (sense 3); the fruit of this plant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "75f351ad-18d7-4d94-92a9-694fd4e1cfc3",
                                                "sense_id": "403fd2e7-d153-3476-8425-e1ea07f98b16",
                                                "text": "The calabash, is a kind of gourd, and belongs to that family of twining plants which were called among the Hebrews, \"wild vines,\" but by the botanists of modern times, the cucurbitaceæ, or cucurbitaceous plants. […] That playful variety of form and magnitude, so remarkable in the calabash, renders it fit for all kinds of uses. Sometimes we have a globular base, terminating in a long neck, and then it answers the purpose of a bottle, and the American fastens it to his girdle, or the pommel of his saddle, when about to pass through regions which abound not in water."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5ac8487-bdde-45a1-a35e-1018bf5051d7",
                                                "sense_id": "403fd2e7-d153-3476-8425-e1ea07f98b16",
                                                "text": "CALABASH GOURD (LAGENARIA SICERARIA) […] Appropriately bowing to AHP, the American Herbal Products Association, for the betterment of the herbal industry, I will now use its standardized common name, Calabash Gourd, a vine, not to be confused with the Calabash tree (Crescentia)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8a1a4e3b-8784-4ba1-ab56-4438a3f4fc99",
                                                "sense_id": "403fd2e7-d153-3476-8425-e1ea07f98b16",
                                                "text": "Asian gourds grow like cucumbers […] and feature strong flavors that are often used in Indian, Chinese, and Southeast Asian soups and stews. Some types to try in your garden include the bitter gourd and calabash gourd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                        "entry_id": "abfec5d9-65b5-3d19-a779-db7e170fc5ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A container made from the mature, dried shell of the fruit of one of the above plants; also, a similarly shaped container made from some other material."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15465228-ada5-4549-a217-36043440470c",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "On Sunday, Oct. 12. being ſtored vvith all things needful for their Journey, viz. Ten Days Proviſion, a Baſin to boil their Provision in, two Calabaſhes to fetch VVater in, and tvvo great Tallipat Leaves for Tents, with Jaggory, Svveet-meats, Tobacco, Betell, Tinder-Boxes, and a Deer-Skin for Shoes, to keep their Feet from Thorns, becauſe to them they chiefly truſted."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "606ce34a-30b1-438b-891f-5d54cdf981ac",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "[T]he manner of separating the gold from the sand, is very simple, and is frequently performed by the women in the middle of the town; for when the searchers return from the valleys in the evening, they commonly bring with them each a calabash or two of sand, to be washed by such of the females as remain at home."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "794be87a-2324-4f60-9ccc-bc2437e33448",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "[page 65] The people of his island of Rokovoko, it seems, at their wedding feasts express the fragrant water of young cocoanuts into a large stained calabash like a punchbowl; and this punchbowl always forms the great central ornament on the braided mat where the feast is held. […] [page 105] [I]t seemed to me that he was dogging us, but with what intent I could not for the life of me imagine. This circumstance, coupled with his ambiguous, half-hinting, half-revealing, shrouded sort of talk, now begat in me all kinds of vague wonderments and half-apprehensions, and all connected with the Pequod; and Captain Ahab; and the leg he had lost; and the Cape Horn fit; and the silver calabash; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec725298-387b-4178-a696-adc11499db3e",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "Saje put the calabash in the king's hands. There was a hush from the crowd. The calabash was large and painted with beautiful designs. Few people had seen it up close."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "411ab461-0f19-456a-a889-03b55ffe4882",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "[...] we would pour water from the tank over ourselves with a calabash and finish by splashing on the Agua Florida from Lanman & Kemps […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6004d2a4-1b8f-4a63-93d7-3d6f6ff3b11c",
                                                "sense_id": "3bb719c1-942a-3eb3-af8f-715f6a1b5569",
                                                "text": "[T]he motorcycle drivers say that new helmets are too expensive and instead have been found wearing pumpkin-like calabashes – dried fruit shells usually used to carry water – cooking pots tied with string or strips of rubber from old tyres."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0c171b3-5a6f-3105-af99-3d24938bc855",
                                        "entry_id": "abfec5d9-65b5-3d19-a779-db7e170fc5ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A calabash and its contents; as much as fills such a container."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b323751c-72ad-4f1c-ba1b-30c2d456fc8a",
                                                "sense_id": "f0c171b3-5a6f-3105-af99-3d24938bc855",
                                                "text": "Amuta and the twelve-year-old have produced calabashes of palm wine and are busy pouring out healthy drams into the cupped hands of black and white alike."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c5f6bfc-58c0-46f7-b512-602826a01414",
                                                "sense_id": "f0c171b3-5a6f-3105-af99-3d24938bc855",
                                                "text": "It was dusk by the time Yandi reappeared, carrying a calabash of parboiled rice and a peanut and chili sauce on his head."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9dc990e4-e063-3def-8986-5f55bfec4484",
                                        "entry_id": "abfec5d9-65b5-3d19-a779-db7e170fc5ab",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A musical instrument, most commonly a drum or rattle, made from a calabash fruit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a90c6652-3d2a-4ac8-8862-b6d3fa61f9e3",
                                                "sense_id": "9dc990e4-e063-3def-8986-5f55bfec4484",
                                                "text": "The inſtrument moſt in requeſt uſed by the Abundi, being the people of the kingdom of Angola, Matamba, and others, is the Marimba; it conſiſts of ſixteen calabaſhes orderly placed along the middle between two ſide-boards joined together, or a long frame, hanging about a man's neck with a thong. Over the mouths of the calabaſhes there are thin ſounding ſlips of red wood called Tanilla, a little above a ſpan long, which being beaten with two little ſticks, returns a ſound from the calabaſhes of ſeveral ſizes not unlike an organ."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
